# Testing Patterns

## Test Structure

```typescript
// ✅ Co-locate tests with source
src/
├── components/
│   ├── button.tsx
│   └── button.test.tsx
├── hooks/
│   ├── use-posts.ts
│   └── use-posts.test.ts
```

## Test Naming

```typescript
describe("usePosts", () => {
  it("should fetch latest post on mount", async () => { });
  it("should handle create mutation success", async () => { });
  it("should invalidate queries after mutation", async () => { });
});
```

## Testing Patterns

```typescript
import { renderHook, waitFor } from "@testing-library/react";
import { usePosts } from "./use-posts";

// ✅ Test user-facing behavior
it("should create post and refetch data", async () => {
  const { result } = renderHook(() => usePosts());

  await result.current.createPost("New Post");

  await waitFor(() => {
    expect(result.current.post?.name).toBe("New Post");
  });
});
```

## Run Tests

```bash
# Unit tests
bun test

# Watch mode
bun test --watch

# UI mode
bun run test:ui
```

## Coverage Goals

- Unit tests: ≥80%
- Integration tests: ≥70%
- E2E tests: Critical paths
